    "summary": "A woman&#039;s outer headscarf, a &#039;kerpa ruva&#039;.  A long, rectangular diaphanous fabric, in two shades of orange.  (One end [42.5 cm wide] is a paler, yellow/orange colour, the same colour as the warp.)  The centre field has regularly spaced fine white bands (grouped in twos).  Tabby woven, with wide, identical patterned borders towards each warp end: two bands of large laid-in diamonds framed by bands of gauze weave and further laid-in work, worked on the diagonal.",
